# JSONata Transform Rules

## Forbidden Patterns

- **No backticks** — they break `dist/handler.js` at runtime. Use `$."field-name"` for special characters.
- **No `//` line comments** — only one-line `/* ... */` block comments. The build strips block comments; line comments break minified output.
- **No template literals** — expressions must be standalone JSONata, no JavaScript.

## Authoring

- Derive transforms from `assets/mapping.json` (the source of truth).
- Request transforms produce the `request_data.inputs` object only — the handler adds the envelope.
- Response transforms receive the full Spark response; use `$.response_data.outputs.field` paths.
- Quote field names containing dashes, dots, or spaces: `$."my-field"`.

## Validation

```bash
node scripts/lint-jsonata.js    # syntax check + test against fixtures
node scripts/validate-mapping.js # validate the mapping document
```

Always run validation after editing transforms. Fix all errors before committing.
